<i>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.600
We've Departed to Space!

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.600
New Chaotix Detectives

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.770
It's so loud! Charmy!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.680
Telephone!

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.730
It's not the phone. It's the doorbell.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.940
It doesn't matter! Just answer it!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.400
You can answer it too, you know.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.700
If it's for a newspaper subscription, we don't want it!

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.570
That sounds like a bad idea for a detective.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.370
You won't keep up with the world's current events.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.910
Who is it?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.830
Hello.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.420
Thank you for coming.

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.880
I'm Vector.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.550
Yes, I know.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.550
Thank you for everything you've done for me.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.890
It's no big deal. It's our job.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.180
Stop flirting. It's disgusting.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.440
Your cake is the best!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.820
There's plenty, so please help yourself.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.530
Thank you.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.240
We won't have to worry about our food expenses!

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.820
Don't talk about things like that!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.700
We haven't had any clients since returning home.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.290
But we're in debt because we rebuilt our office.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.290
We're in financial trouble again this month.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.840
I'll bring something more filling next time.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.010
Thank you!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.220
I accept your offer!

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.180
Sure.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.180
Espio, this isn't how your character acts.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.850
Your cake is the best!

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.520
Thank you very much.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.110
Baking them was worth the trouble because you're so happy.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.940
I ate Cream's cake before.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.280
I now understand why her cake was so delicious.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.660
You must be a good teacher!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.990
Vector, you're very good at flattery.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:53.580
Now I know why Cream is recently making sweets and cakes everyday.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:57.130
She enjoyed receiving compliments from everyone.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.260
She's baking everyday?

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.340
Yes, everyday.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:09.850
Since coming home, how's everyone doing?

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.230
It's the same as usual.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.550
Episode 78

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.550
The Place where Planets are Born

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:22.070
Mama and I baked this cake together.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.030
She also took some to Vector today.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.280
For them? What a waste.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.580
How about you, Amy?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.500
This!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.120
Wow! Apple pie! It looks delicious!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.790
It's Ella's special recipe.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.380
Pretty good, right?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:43.760
With all these sweets, Tails is going to get fat.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.010
Yeah. He may lose his ability to fly.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.680
What did he say?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.890
If that happens, he wants to race Tails.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.100
Cheese will definitely win.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.440
After filling his stomach with delicious food, he has to exercise.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.530
He has to run hard and fly around.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:09.160
And will that cheer him up?

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.120
It has to.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:41.020
When it regains its lost energy, it should naturally return to normal.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.480
Are you going to do what you usually do?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.360
Please, Master Emerald! Return to your original state!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.280
You mean that?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.410
Yeah.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.160
So, Knuckles...

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.870
I won't do that.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:58.830
I don't know how long it will take, but I'll wait and relax until it returns to normal.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.300
I want to give it all the rest it needs.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.800
It worked really hard for us.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.560
You're right.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:21.650
I want to build a house, but how do I do that in this world?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.980
Huh? We build houses differently in this world than in yours?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.940
I'm not talking about the construction process.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:30.870
For the size and location, do I need to get everyone's permission?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.580
What are you talking about? Build it wherever there's space.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.210
But what if the land belongs to someone?

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.380
Someone's land? Is his name written in the ground?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.090
Chris, are names written in the ground in your world?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.760
Well...

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:54.310
It's not literally written, but the land belongs to the owner.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.350
What a chore.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:01.810
That means you'll have to decide who owns the sky and the ocean someday.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.940
Yeah.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.230
Why do you want a house?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.070
I can't stay at Cream's house forever.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:15.490
I've been sleeping outdoors all my life.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.040
Sleeping outdoors is great!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:22.460
Rainy days can be a hassle, but I can feel the seasons changing firsthand.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.040
The grass is my pillow, and the stars are my roof.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.460
What do you think?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.130
I want a normal roof.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:33.760
I see.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.900
This is unexpected.

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.110
You're still worried about him?

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.570
Not really.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.660
I'm just wondering where he is.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.450
Who knows...

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.910
Well, I don't think there's anything to worry about.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:07.630
Because my grandfather, known as the scientist of the century, created the ultimate life form.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.510
Do you really think he's...

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.680
You have big boobs.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:29.440
It's time for you to leave. This ship is being retired.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.500
Tails!

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.000
Hi!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.420
When we came home, we settled into a peaceful routine.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.550
I've experienced days like this in the past.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:08.270
Though we feel like nothing is changing, time still passes by.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.900
Everything passes on, like a dream.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:23.450
But there's something that can never vanish...

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.900
Cosmo!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:02.220
Thank you for stopping us.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:11.150
I always thought that I was useless and had no strength.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.320
That I couldn't do anything for anyone.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:24.080
But now, I finally understand!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.750
No matter what happens, these feelings I have will never vanish.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.090
Forever and ever...

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.310
I'll be by your side forever.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.750
Cosmo...

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.210
Chaos...

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:22.510
Regeneration!

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:36.360
How strange. This light feels familiar.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.360
It's kind...

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:43.490
...and a little sad.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.200
Oh no!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:50.370
There's an abnormality! The Planet Eggs' power will erupt at once!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.160
Use the Emergency Egg Drive!

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.170
Dr. Eggman, did you forget?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.670
Just a little while ago...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:00.460
We used all our remaining energy, idiot.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.340
Oh yeah. Then we're in trouble.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:11.930
I see. Now that the Planet Eggs are free, they'll simultaneously release their power.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.270
I have to do this!

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.390
Chaos-

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.360
Shadow...

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:33.330
Since your Chaos Control is horrible, I can't let you do this.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.380
Chaos Control!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:53.930
What happened?

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.140
He vanished.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:58.860
Shadow...

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.780
Something is shining!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.200
Dr. Eggman, what is that?

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.280
He must have also stopped time.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.990
The time lag is too great for this distance.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.370
So that's what we were fighting a moment ago?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:20.380
That's right. I don't think you need me to explain who did what.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.010
Chaos Control.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:27.300
He used Chaos Control even though he didn't have much strength left.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.140
That means...

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.110
Sonic!

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:53.660
Sonic, umm...

00:14:54.790 --> 00:15:00.750
Tails, this was all that was left.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.510
It's not true!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.970
Cosmo was just here!

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.730
I heard her voice...

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:29.200
Sonic, I had faith that you would save her!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.320
I believed in you!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.380
Wow.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.340
It's like a meteor shower.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:50.010
It's beautiful... It's beautifully sad.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.300
They're all Planet Eggs?

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:59.020
They're returning to their homes.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.190
Man, I sounded cool!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:03.100
He's blushing.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.770
It's because your dialogue didn't match your character!

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.900
You didn't act like your characters either!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.440
What are you talking about? I always act like this.

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:10.860
Me too. This is the real me.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.700
Liar!

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:13.870
That's why I hate acting with amateurs!

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.490
You still have much to learn!

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.910
You don't know how to get deep into character.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.290
You guys annoy me!

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:24.210
Hey, prepare to recharge our energy. We're going home.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.380
Okay!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.020
Hey, man-boy!

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:43.940
Will you stop calling me that?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.650
Don't let it bother you, idiot!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.820
Look! I'm carrying a bag for the first time in awhile!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.570
I feel more at home!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.530
Here.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.200
Why are you hiding?

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:54.820
Because...

00:16:54.820 --> 00:17:00.330
No "because"! Dr. Eggman told me to deliver this to you!

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:01.290
Eggman?

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:13.840
The controller of light, has your wish been granted?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.680
The true nature of animals won't change.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:25.020
You cut down trees, destroy planets and will eventually annihilate the universe.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:33.190
Next time, our descendants will fix the future.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:39.200
Will you still try to stop us?

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:41.740
Of course.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:48.840
Because I still want to keep running free on my own two feet.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:52.260
Good night! Have sweet dreams!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.910
Eggman, what's this about?

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.450
What don't you understand?

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.990
It's all written there.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:26.580
It says that it's a one-way ticket to Earth.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:31.170
Dr. Eggman fiddled around and figured it out.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.510
Unlike you, he has brains.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:36.880
That means this machine is...

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.840
It's a teleporter to take you back to your world.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.510
That's right. I named it...

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.680
Hurry Up and Go Home Version 1!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.810
There's only enough energy for a one-way trip.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:54.280
All it can do is take you back to your world, but that shouldn't be a problem.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:57.610
Why are you doing this for me?

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.160
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.280
I built this because I thought it would be fun.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.490
Huh?

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:08.000
This machine can take you home.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.830
But I never said that you'll arrive home at the same age.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.210
You might be 18 years old again.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.340
Or you might shrink even more and become 6 years old.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.970
Or you might even become a baby!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.470
It's so thrilling!

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:25.810
Even if I can't return to my original age, I don't want to shrink even more.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.850
Then what will you do? Will you not go?

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.020
I'll go.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.230
I trust your machine, Eggman.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.690
Way to ruin the mood, idiot.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:40.200
This scene wasn't supposed to be a tearjerker.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.570
How could you trust a villain?

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:45.410
It's fine, but this next statement will surprise you.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.080
You only have three minutes left until you leave!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:49.910
What?

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.870
That statement was effective!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.630
You can't say goodbye to everyone!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.550
That was nice timing, wasn't it?

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.050
I understand.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:58.920
What?

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.430
Stop fooling around!

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.720
You're going to leave without saying goodbye?

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.760
You're cold-hearted!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.890
I'm disappointed in you!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:10.230
I promise I'll come back.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.440
Are you really going to trust this guy?

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:16.480
He may be lying!

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.440
You still might have a chance!

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.660
Yeah! Maybe you can have a farewell party before you leave!

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.870
He can't.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:30.160
Three minutes from now, the planetary motion and magnetic interference will be ideal.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:34.880
That's when the two worlds will connect in space and time. It's destiny.

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:36.170
Destiny?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.380
Time, location, people...

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:43.890
Destiny decides the fate of all things.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:48.640
I was able to come to this world because of destiny?

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.060
Most likely.

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.730
Destiny also allowed me to revive Shadow.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:56.400
Even Dark Oak's forestation was a thousand year-old destiny.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:00.190
You giving me a one-way ticket is also destiny?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:04.610
If you want to change it into a round-trip ticket, then you have to work for it yourself!

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.910
You can live here!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:10.790
If you don't want to be my minion, then I'll let you be the same rank as me!

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.790
That means they'll be our minions!

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.210
What are you talking about?

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.420
Since when did we become your minions?

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:22.220
The least you could do is say thank you before leaving!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:27.970
I'm going to lie and tell your friends that you left happily...

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.640
That you couldn't wait to go home...

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:37.310
Idiot!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:50.240
I left in a hurry. I wonder if everyone will be angry...

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:51.700
What? He went home?

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.370
How could he!

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.290
He didn't even say goodbye...

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:59.630
He said we'd build a new Typhoon together!

00:22:00.170 --> 00:22:02.300
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:20.900
Sonic...

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:24.280
Sonic...

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:46.300
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:46.300
<i><i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i></i>

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:38.620
Sonic!

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:40.020
<i>Original Concept Created by</i>

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:44.030
<i>Executive Producer</i>

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:47.860
<i>Producer</i>

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:55.060
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:55.060
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>Animation Producer</i>

00:22:52.660 --> 00:22:55.600
<i>Associate Producer</i>

00:22:55.060 --> 00:23:04.150
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:22:55.060 --> 00:23:04.150
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>Story Editor</i>

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.690
All right!

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:03.210
<i>Supervisors</i>

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:03.650
We have one less person interfering with our plans!

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:07.570
Let's restart building the Eggman Empire!

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:14.080
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:14.080
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:07.050
<i>Directed by</i>

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:09.740
Roger!

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:11.050
<i>Original Characters Created by</i>

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:14.890
<i>Character Design</i>

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:14.890
<i>Animation Director</i>

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.200
What? Eggman is at it again?

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:22.790
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:22.790
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:18.710
<i>Mechanical Design</i>

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.420
Can't he just give up already?

00:23:19.690 --> 00:23:22.560
<i>Art Director</i>

00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:24.340
What a nuisance!

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:26.070
<i>Sound Director</i>

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:32.640
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:32.640
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:27.030 --> 00:23:30.740
<i>French Adaption</i>

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:31.640
I'll go tease him.

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:42.190
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:42.190
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.540
<i>Sound Production</i>

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:42.020
Everyone, get on board! Let's go!

00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:43.420
<i>Music</i>

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:50.610
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:50.610
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:47.210
<i>Editor</i>

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:47.360
I won't forgive you, Eggman!

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:51.050
<i>Produced by</i>

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:55.410
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:55.410
<i>Forever...</i>
